# https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# WHY THIS FILE. The constrained-decoding work here is citable — a schema-derived
# pushdown automaton with a per-step logit mask, plus a termination bound that
# the category does not usually advertise, plus a measurement that runs the other
# way from the format-tax literature on tool selection. None of that could be
# cited before, because there was nothing to cite. GitHub reads this file and
# offers "Cite this repository" from it.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Tacet in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "Tacet: constrained tool calling for local language models"
abstract: >-
  A local-first assistant whose tool calls are constrained rather than validated:
  the argument schema is compiled into a pushdown automaton and every generation
  step is masked, so a call the schema forbids cannot be produced. The constraint
  contract is three signatures over a logit slice and a token id, in a crate with
  no inference dependency, so any runtime can take the guarantee without taking
  an engine. Two further claims are measured rather than asserted: that a valid
  call must terminate (bounded whitespace, a bounded open field, a token cap),
  and that no data leaves the device (exactly two of eleven crates declare an
  HTTP dependency, checked by a test).
type: software
